<meta type=article>
<title | Section numbering with a contents listing (#218)>
<author | The Enscribe Team>
</meta>

<config number-sections=true toc=true toc-location=body />

<section #sec:intro | Introduction>

Numbering is config-driven (`<config number-sections=true>`), stamped in the shared
runSync so the static build and the live render number identically. The numbers are
hierarchical — 1, 1.1, 1.1.1 — and (with a contents listing on) they show in the listing,
reusing the un-glue path.

<sub-section | Background>

A level-2 heading, numbered 1.1.

<sub-sub-section | Prior work>

A level-3 heading, numbered 1.1.1.

<section +unnumbered | A Note on Notation>

An `+unnumbered` heading — outside the numbered sequence: it gets no number, and the
counter does not advance, so the next section continues unbroken. (It is still *listed*
— `+unnumbered` is numbering-only; `+unlisted` is the listing override.)

<section | Methods>

Numbered 2 — the unnumbered section above did not advance the counter.
